## Story Description
CategoryPage crashes when selectedL2 is set but selectedL2Entry is null (e.g. after a filter change resets the hierarchy). The l3Rows computation at line ~164 needs a null guard. Also add an explicit Back button that appears whenever selectedL1 is set, giving users a clear way to return to the category overview without needing to know about the DrilldownBreadcrumb.

## Acceptance Criteria
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/CategoryPage.tsx — guard the l3Rows line to: const l3Rows = (selectedL1Entry && selectedL2Entry) ? [...selectedL2Entry.l3s].sort((a, b) => (b.total_spend ?? 0) - (a.total_spend ?? 0)) : []
- Edit file: frontend/src/pages/dashboard/CategoryPage.tsx — add an ArrowLeft import from lucide-react (if not already imported); render a Back button immediately above the KPI cards section (when selectedL1 is non-null): <Button variant='outline' size='sm' className='mb-4' onClick={() => { setSelectedL1(null); setSelectedL2(null) }}><ArrowLeft className='h-4 w-4 mr-1' />All Categories</Button>
- When selectedL2 is set and the Back button is clicked, both selectedL1 and selectedL2 are cleared and the overview scorecard table is shown again
- Run: cd frontend && npx tsc --noEmit — exits with code 0

